# Per-device UI, shared behavior

- **Visual changes** (layout, color, spacing, type, chrome): scope CSS to the selected preview with `html[data-device="iphone"]`, `html[data-device="ipad"]`, or `html[data-device="desktop"]`. Put overrides in `app/device-ui.css`. Infer the device from the user's last shell (iPhone / iPad / Desktop), `knDevice` in the iframe URL, or `localStorage kn-device`.
- **Do not** restyle all devices when the user is iterating on one shell.
- **Functionality** (save, login, search, navigation, data, handlers): edit shared TS/TSX components only. Every shell uses the same actions.

```css
/* UI for iPhone only */
html[data-device="iphone"] .mktHero h1 { font-size: 36px; }
```

```tsx
/* Shared action — all devices */
function onSave(e: MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) {
  e.preventDefault();
  router.push("/login?next=/saved");
}
```
